Third-party material
====================

1. paypaldev/hackathon-paypal-ag-grid-boilerplate
   https://github.com/paypaldev/hackathon-paypal-ag-grid-boilerplate (commit 5de114e, 2026-10-12)
   (c) PayPal. No licence declared (GitHub reports `license: null`, checked 2026-11-10).
   It is the official boilerplate of the PayPal AI Hackathon and is used here under the hackathon's
   rules, as a reference. Files copied from it or closely derived from it:

   - lib/studio/openai-adapter.ts
       Copied from the boilerplate's app/dashboard/studio/openai-adapter.ts, which is itself copied
       verbatim from the AG Studio documentation example (Direct LLM Runner).
   - lib/paypal/client.ts
       Our own code; its behaviour (OAuth client-credentials token caching, paging, retries on
       401/429/5xx) is modelled on the boilerplate's lib/paypal.ts.
   - app/api/ai/responses/route.ts and lib/ai/config.ts
       Our own code modelled on the boilerplate's OpenAI proxy (model allowlist, output-token cap,
       SSE pass-through). Adds passcode auth, per-IP rate limiting and a daily spend cap.

